WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.642
Serialized data often lives longer and travels farther than developers
expect.

2
00:00:04.642 --> 00:00:11.468
It may be stored in files, databases, caches, queues, object storage,
logs, backups, artifacts, and support bundles.

3
00:00:11.468 --> 00:00:14.608
Before serializing, ask whether each field is needed.

4
00:00:14.608 --> 00:00:23.756
Data minimization reduces exposure by avoiding unnecessary secrets,
tokens, credentials, personal data, regulated data, and business
confidential data.

5
00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:26.623
Privacy-aware logging is especially important.

6
00:00:26.623 --> 00:00:32.903
Logs are searchable, copied, retained, and sometimes accessible to more
people than production databases.

7
00:00:32.903 --> 00:00:40.207
Safe audit events should capture meaningful security and operational
activity without dumping entire serialized payloads.

8
00:00:40.207 --> 00:00:47.990
When errors occur, messages should identify the validation problem without
exposing sensitive content or parser internals to users.

9
00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:51.744
Retention and deletion rules should include serialized copies.

10
00:00:51.744 --> 00:01:00.277
A sensitive field removed from the primary database may still exist in
queues, caches, logs, backups, analytics exports, and debugging artifacts.

11
00:01:00.277 --> 00:01:10.858
Safe serialization design includes where data is stored, how long it
remains, who can read it, whether it is encrypted or access-controlled,
and how deletion or expiration is handled.

12
00:01:10.858 --> 00:01:14.203
Testing and review make serialization controls durable.

13
00:01:14.203 --> 00:01:25.125
Useful tests include malformed input, oversized input, unknown fields,
wrong types, stale versions, rejected advanced features, privacy checks,
and deserialization regression tests.

14
00:01:25.125 --> 00:01:35.160
Code review should ask where the data came from, what parser settings are
used, what schema is enforced, what is logged, and whether object
reconstruction is truly necessary.
